  data: {
    LLM: "Standard Whist principles apply: lead from your longest suit, support partner's leads, save trumps for capturing high cards. The Dummy exposure gives the declaring side a major information advantage.\n\nTrump declaration strategy: with a strong suit of 5+ cards, declare that suit. With balanced strength and high cards across suits, declare 'biritch' (no-trump) to maximise the value of standalone Aces and Kings.\n\nContreing: challenge the opponents' declaration if you hold strong trumps or length in their declared suit. The risk/reward of contre vs. sur-contre adds a psychological dimension absent from regular Whist. Reading the Dummy: after the Dummy is exposed, the lead player can see 26 of 52 cards â€” use this to plan a precise line of attack.",
